Полиморфизм позволяет одному участку про:
Polymorphism allows one section of a program to operate on different objects through a consistent operation. Here two formatters provide `render(text)` and the generic code does not check their specific class. This example does not require inheritance.

```python
class Upper:
    def render(self, text):
        return text.upper()

class Brackets:
    def render(self, text):
        return f'[{text}]'

for formatter in [Upper(), Brackets()]:
    print(formatter.render('Python'))
```

```text
PYTHON
[Python]
```

Both methods accept text and return text. If one of them starts printing and returning `None`, the general agreement will be broken. The same method name is not enough: the meaning, valid arguments, and expected result must match.

При обычном запуске файла его `__name__`:
When a file is launched normally, its `__name__` value is `'__main__'`. When importing, the name of the module. Validation allows you to provide functions for reuse and separately execute the main script only when the file is run.

```python
def format_title(text):
    return text.strip().title()

def main():
    print(format_title('  python lab  '))

if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
```

```text
